[Music]  hello there free to play games are  slowly taking over the triple a video  game world top quality creations without  an entry fee 2022 promises to be a crazy  year for new free-to-play games and as  long as you keep in mind they will try  to take your money through other means  like in-game items cosmetics and other  micro transactions you are good to go so  let's see what 2022 has in store for us  first up is rumble verse yet another  battle royale but wait this one has a  trick up its sleeve rumble verse is a  brawler royale all the moves are more  like a typical wwe match than a game of  fortnite ultra cartoony physics are used  with every building and structure being  scalable and vehicles are effectively  trampolines 40 players are freely  running around the city waiting to lay  the smacketh down on each other i've got  to admit it looks good to me  customization is a key selling point in  rumble verse with hundreds of items of  clothing body shapes and designer gear  to unlock and by allowing us all to  design our characters from head to toe  do what you like embrace your inner  furry become a member of team thick or  build whatever monstrosity you want the  options may be limitless rumbleverse  will be using open and paid closed betas  to perfect the game before suddenly  releasing completely free to play on all  platforms sometime in 2022  [Music]  next we have tom clancy's ex-defiant a  free-to-play arena shooter combining  numerous tom clancy worlds into one big  mosh pit ubisoft are taking the  realistic shooting from rainbow six  siege and merging that with the  superpowers of games like valorant and  overwatch each character in the team has  an ability which changes the game  slightly a hollow shield for defense an  armored turret for support and an  invisibility suit to sneak around all  these add to each fight making them more  tactical and also complete bedlam fans  of the division splinter cell and ghost  recon are all represented with factions  beginning with these four wolves who  have tank abilities the outcasts who  have healing abilities echelon have  night vision goggles and other tech and  the cleaners have crazy high dps  xdefiant and ubisoft should give us more  information in early 2022  game three arc raiders a co-operative  free-to-play third-person shooter where  you and your squad of raiders unite to  resist the onslaught of ark a ruthless  mechanized threat descending from space  taken from the book of the same name we  are a member of the resistance force  eliminating all the threats we can the  book has lots of time travel to contend  with but that's unclear if it's part of  the game too arc raiders is deliberately  set up to make going in alone highly  dangerous and only a cooperative squad  is the right way to play this a full  troop of your friends with comms all  playing completely for free taking down  giant alien spider bots or shooting  scutters out of the sky arc raiders  could be huge we'll see more later in  2022  out of nowhere someone is trying to take  on super mario kart take a look at kart  rider's drift this is actually not a new  game this series has been operating as a  free-to-play title with  microtransactions for many years over in  the east but now it's coming over to the  west challenge your friends regardless  of what platform they play on and enjoy  no barriers or paywalls to play the core  game created to be a completely online  game when new additions race tracks and  modes are added constantly the plan is  for the full game to release with at  least 100 carts and over 150 character  outfits showing us that customization is  once again the most direct way to get  into our wallets it remains to be seen  if there is a karting audience outside  of nintendo this could be the year cart  rider drift  [Music]  back in 2016 let it die released on the  ps4 and later came to pc an action  role-playing game with elements of dark  souls and a bucket load of grind to  progress mechanics fast forward six  years and that game world is being  expanded via death verse let it die  set in the format of a tv show  contestants fight to the death so yes  it's another battle royale this time  though it's melee focused we've seen a  whole heap of weird and wonderful  weapons from a superman dive with  oversized gauntlets and a deep sea diver  with a hammer bigger than your mum it's  a weird place this death verse release  date is set for spring so expect this to  first release on playstation around  march to june time and if the previous  game is anything to go by it will come  to pc soon after  here's a game i have high hopes for  multiverses let's get the most obvious  thing out of the way this is another  game which wants to be nintendo this  time smash bros a competitive platform  fighter that is totally free to play  although single player mode is here the  game is firmly based on team mechanics  for example batman's smoke bomb can hide  his allies steven shield can do exactly  that protect the squad and wonder  woman's kinky whip of truth can save a  falling friend effectively each  character has abilities to enhance each  fight multiverses takes warner brothers  properties and smashes them together  like arya stark from game of thrones who  could fight shaggy from scooby-doo it  doesn't make any sense at all but it  could be great if multiverses becomes  popular we can expect other warner bros  movies and games to be added the  potential is limitless from all the  games on the list multiverses looks the  most complete and ready to go in 2022 it  really could be the breakout  free-to-play game of the year  back over to ubisoft who has five  free-to-play games coming out over the  next few years this one is the division  heartland due out in 2022 we've heard  nothing since they first announced it  and we still don't even know if this  will be a third person shooter like the  rest of the division series we do know  that heartland is a standalone game that  doesn't require any previous experience  of the series as it will take us on a  new journey and a new perspective on the  universe many people are suggesting  heartland will be another battle royale  but there is no proof of this yet  whatever it becomes i'll be sure to make  a video on it later in the year so throw  me a sub if you'd be so kind i'd like to  get to two million and pretend my life  means something  [Music]  so that ubisoft game is uncertain so  let's switch to another one ghost recon  front line this one certainly is a third  person online shooter the blurb says  ghost recon frontline features an  advanced class system and a large set of  tactical support tools allowing for  complete freedom in strategic gameplay  with multiple ways to outsmart enemy  teams and win every fight like usual the  blurb that comes with games is so  confusing many people believe that this  game will be more like escape from  tarkov where a team of operatives go  into a map against other players and try  to come out again with new tech and  intel then rinse and repeat sadly this  game was thrown into limbo late in 2021  as the community was just not happy  ubisoft didn't have a good time with  free-to-play games last year so the beta  4 frontline was delayed until 2022 we'll  have more confirmation soon and the only  thing we do know is that it won't run on  last gen consoles on your pc ps5 and the  xbox series  many of these games are without a  certain release date right now so here's  a certain one for january pubg the  battle royale which was arguably the  first to make the genre a worldwide  phenomenon on january 12th it finally  goes free to play i don't think you need  me to break this down but without this  game we probably wouldn't have fortnite  so give it a try jump out of the plane  pick up a weapon or a frying pan and get  the vic roy by being the last to survive  i mean win a winner chicken dinner  hey you have you ever wanted to ride a  dragon then you should check out century  age of ashes it released on pc late 2021  and is coming to console in 2022 age of  ashes is a pretty intense fight or  flight survival game the game mode  scenes so far are three on three are six  versus six all all-air combat on the  back of dragons each class has a certain  play style wind guard phantom and  marauder with unique abilities too for  example the phantoms have a mine ability  and the marauders can wield frost bolts  a multiplayer dragon battle game who'd  have thunk it  [Music]  for the next bunch of games we're going  to go much quicker as most of these were  supposedly releasing in 2021 but they  never did when they do though i will  release a breakdown video more in detail  but for now we're going to rush through  it roller champions remember this game  back in 2019 we saw this and in 2021 it  was about to release and then suddenly  vanished the idea of the game is pretty  simple grab a ball throw it through a  hoop and each lap of the course you  complete determines how many points that  ball is worth the game was delayed for  extra polish to be added whatever that  means so we should see it in 2022 knives  out knives out is a popular mobile game  in the same vein as pubg and has been  coming to console for years it now has  2022 on its radar with the confirmation  that knives out extreme is confirmed and  it was confirmed by playstation it's  more battle royale you either like it or  you're absolutely sick of that genre by  now next blood hunt if you know my  channel you know blood hunt a vampire  focused battle royale was scheduled to  release on ps5 over halloween it missed  that deadline it was then promised to  arrive in 2021 and it's missed that  deadline too and now the new date is  spring 2022 so expect this between march  and june if you don't want to wait that  long it's also available on pc right now  scavengers another game i had such high  hopes for a post-apocalypse survival  battle royale with pve elements too  surviving the cold weather while slaying  falls looked insanely fun scavengers did  make it to pc in 2021 yet consoles are  waiting for the full release which comes  in 22. next caliber another one of the  games we hope to see in 2021 and like  scavengers it did release on pc the  free-to-play tactical military shooter  has a small but loyal fan base and in  2022 we should see the full release of  the game including next gen consoles so  watch this space  [Music]  and finally league of legends wild rift  with the exceptional arcane netflix show  bringing us so many league characters  many console players have been waiting  to try league of legends wild rift the  mobile version of the online battle  arena was due to come to consoles in  2020 but due to the outbreak we can't  talk about on youtube progress was  stopped and the release date for  consoles was completely taken away with  2022 here is it finally time to see  league of legends on console if not you  can always play on mobile and pc right  now so there we have it 16 free-to-play  games coming in 2022 well 15 in league  of legends wild rift are there any of  these you'd like me to cover in more  depth because i'm happy to do so just  need to let me know if you're watching  this before christmas please have a good  one but if not have a great year 2022 is  your year i'm adam you're awesome i'm  taking the week off woohoo see you soon  bye  [Music]

